> ## Guffin Contribution Checklist: Sampling/Cache Logic Changes

**Goal:** Ensure correctness and performance of modified sampling or cache logic.

**I. Automated Correctness Checks (Mandatory)**

*   [ ] **Lossless Probability:** Run `make test` – specifically, verify `tests/engine/lossless_sampling_tests.cpp` passes. Ensure the new logic maintains the configured sampling distribution.
*   [ ] **Numerical Integrity:** Run `make test` – focus on `tests/tensor/gemma3_metal_tests.cpp`. Confirm packed projections, fused sums, and floating-point operations remain numerically accurate.
*   [ ] **Cache Synchronization:** Run `make test` – verify `tests/engine/gemma2_metal_plan_tests.cpp` passes. Confirm target/draft caches & callback receipts remain synchronized.
*   [ ] **Tensor Validation:** Run `make test` – check `tests/tensor/tensor_tests.cpp`. Ensure descriptors validate and views check backing storage.
*   [ ] **Code Review:** Address all reviewer comments, focusing on ownership, resource lifetimes, and explicit dependencies.

**II. Actual-Chat Performance Measurements (Highly Recommended)**

*   [ ] **Define Baseline:** Record existing performance (tokens/s, TTFT) from the `Performance` section (currently pending).
*   [ ] **Implement Measurement:** Add instrumentation to the new code to track key metrics.
*   [ ] **Run Benchmarks:** Execute the modified code on representative prompts.
*   [ ] **Compare Performance:**  Does the change improve end-to-end chat performance beyond statistical noise? If not, reconsider.
*   [ ] **Document Findings:** Record prompt, model, settings, and timings in `docs/PERFORMANCE.md`.



**Important Notes:**

*   Adhere to `ENGINE_PRINCIPLES.md` regarding independent numerical references & avoiding production dependencies for validation.
*   Consult `docs/ENGINE_PRINCIPLES.md` and `docs/NEXT_TASK.md` for architectural guidelines.
